A colon form that is no SSL keyword (`:ELSEIF`, borrowed from other
languages) in a position where it stands alone as a statement:
unknown_keyword (warning) names it verbatim. Because unknown_keyword is a
warning, unexpected_token does not defer where the grammar fails, and
the block pairing is unaffected (diag.unknown_keyword).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE SizeBand;
	:PARAMETERS nSize;
	:DECLARE sBand;
	:IF nSize < 10;
		sBand := "S";
	:ELSEIF;
		sBand := "M";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sBand;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE SizeBand;
	:PARAMETERS nSize;
	:DECLARE sBand;

	:IF nSize < 10;
		sBand := "S";
		:ELSEIF;
		sBand := "M";
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN sBand;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:2-6:9 warning unknown_keyword: Unknown SSL keyword: ':ELSEIF'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:2-6:9 warning unknown_keyword: Unknown SSL keyword: ':ELSEIF'
